@startuml
title Maturity semantic rule and pattern support - target conceptual flow
rectangle "Evidence and signals" as evidence
rectangle "JSON definitions and\nexecutable conditions" as rules
rectangle "Rule evaluation" as match
rectangle "Pattern aggregation" as aggregate
rectangle "Evidence sufficiency,\nsupport and challenge" as support
rectangle "Insight candidate" as candidate
rectangle "Trace: provenance,\nstates and reasons" as trace
evidence --> match
rules --> match
match --> aggregate : triggered rules
aggregate --> support
evidence --> support
support --> candidate : only when eligible
match ..> trace
aggregate ..> trace
support ..> trace
note bottom of match
  Semantic evidence may be matched directly.
  A trigger does not establish sufficient support.
  Reuse of BehaviourRuleEngine is an open option.
  Numeric flow rules use a distinct strategy and schema.
end note
@enduml
